{
 "v": "aumlok-pleasant-drop-v1",
 "what": "X2's pleasantness pass: the words an AUMLOK band or anchor may NOT be drawn from, beyond the profanity block and the category drops, because a phrase a person memorises for life should not be built out of them.",
 "filterRole": "FILTER, NOT SOURCE. This file can only ever REMOVE a candidate word. No word reaches a shipped list from here.",
 "provenance": {
  "kind": "CURATED JUDGMENT LIST — NOT A PUBLISHED SOURCE",
  "author": "item X2 of `## PETER'S FIRST REAL BIND` (.agents/live/rounds/AUMLOK.md), 2026-09-23",
  "saysSo": "This is a hand-judged list written for this repository. It is deliberately NOT attributed to a published source, because it is not one: no dictionary, corpus, wordlist or web service produced it, and it carries no third-party licence. Its authority is the judgment recorded in the commit that landed it, and a reviewer is meant to disagree with individual entries — that is what a judgment list is for. It is named by category so a disagreement can name the entry it is about.",
  "how": "Every entry was read against the words the X2 rebuild actually shipped, in the order the harvest prints: the coordinator's own flagged draws (`direness`, `corroding`, `pungent`, `seduce`, `travesty`, `epidermis`, `delouse`, `outhouse`, `hemlock`, `batboy`, `snowiness`, `pettiness`, `rocklike`, `superjet`, `eastcoast`, `tipoff`, `unglue`) were placed first, and each category was then walked through the surviving pool a word at a time.",
  "limits": "NOT complete, and it does not claim to be. Judgment about a word is not a property a list can exhaust, and a word not named here is not thereby endorsed. Its measured effect is in the harvest ladder and in the shipped data provenance, not asserted here."
 },
 "conventions": {
  "rolesAreNotSymptoms": "A medical or martial ROLE is not dropped by this file: `nurse`, `doctor`, `sailor`, `chef` are things people do, which the UNITE band is FOR. What is dropped is the affliction, the disease, the weapon and the corpse.",
  "animalsAreNotVermin": "An animal is a ROOT word, not a disgust word. Only the vermin and parasite families (rat, roach, maggot, flea, lice, worm, vulture) are dropped here."
 },
